# Force CRLF line endings on Windows-native batch files. Without this,
# contributors with core.autocrlf=false (or input) can unknowingly
# commit LF-only versions, which makes cmd.exe fail batch parsing with
# the cryptic  "': was unexpected at this time.'"  error.
#
# Everything else stays LF — bash heredocs, build/*.sh, src/*, etc.
*.bat   text eol=crlf
*.cmd   text eol=crlf
